Question No: 322. Coin Change

Solution is Written in C++ Language.

Solution:

class Solution {
public:
    int coinChange(vector<int>& coins, int amount) {
        vector<int> minCoins(amount + 1, amount + 1);
        minCoins[0] = 0;

        for (int i = 1; i <= amount; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < coins.size(); j++) {
                if (i - coins[j] >= 0) {
                    minCoins[i] = min(minCoins[i], 1 + minCoins[i - coins[j]]);
                }
            }
        }

        return minCoins[amount] != amount + 1 ? minCoins[amount] : -1;        
    }
};


Approach:

Initialize DP array: Create minCoins of size amount + 1, initialized to amount + 1 (a value representing infinity).

Base case: Set minCoins[0] = 0, since 0 coins are needed to make amount 0.

Iterate through amounts: Loop from 1 to amount.

Check each coin: For every amount, try all available coins.

Update minimum: If i - coins[j] >= 0, update: minCoins[i] = min(minCoins[i], 1 + minCoins[i - coins[j]])

Return result: If the target amount is achievable, return minCoins[amount]; otherwise, return -1.
